{"kind":"assert","text":"Additional blocking evidence for the changes-requested review of chess item 3 exact head 090f3416. First, the public contract says a repository is bound to one application for life and upgrades replace only the source/fold, but BindingInForce accepts the last initializer-signed Binding even when Application changes; the existing later-binding test deliberately permits Workroom-to-other-application migration. Preserve the initial/default application identity and allow only an upgrade within it. Second, an outside module cannot open an ordinary clone or attached read-only copy: host.Open requires repository-private config.json, apphost is internal, and host exports no attach or open-by-genesis act. The governing design says any clone can replay and deployment clones the data repository at boot. Expose the minimal bounded read-only attach/open path or explicitly narrow the promised clone/deployment contract, and prove it from the second-module test. These findings supplement report 5f422357; they are not a duplicate verdict."}